# Domovoi

## Lore

The Domovoi is the Russian house goblin: two feet tall, covered head to toe in
dark brown or black fur except for hands, feet and face, with a bushy beard and
an unruly mane. It adopts a house and the family inside it, considers itself an
unofficial part of that family, and stays for generations.

It milks the cow, chops wood, sweeps the floor, puts out small fires and
frightens off predators, and it warns the household of danger by stirring up the
animals or banging on the pots. The big inhabitants are expected to reciprocate
with a bowl of porridge and something sweet.

It avoids adults and appears to children, who it watches over and pulls back
from wells and riversides. A parent or relative who is cruel to a child earns a
thorn in the shoe, a broken possession, a push down the stairs. If that person
kills the child, the Domovoi may kill them - and it never kills in an obvious
way. The death looks like an accident.

## Alignment

Any, but the majority are unprincipled (40%) or anarchist (30%).

## GM Notes

**The book''s Player Note is a permission, not an invitation.** A Domovoi is
allowable as an optional player character, but it says outright that the
character will be extremely limited in its range of skills and abilities, and
that **95% of Domovoi dislike and abstain from adventure**. A player taking one
is playing against the grain of the species.

It is the only one of the six imported Woodland Spirits with **no psionics at
all**, and it is the smallest and weakest of them - the Leshii is ten feet tall
and the Spirit Wolf runs at 82 mph.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'domovoi');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'domovoi';

